

# ── Subject: <scope>: what changed, imperative, ~60 chars ────────────────────
# 71% of this repo uses a "<scope>: " prefix. Not Conventional Commits — that
# was considered and rejected (only 12% of history, and its payoff is automated
# changelog and semver, neither of which this project wants).
#
# ── Body: why, not what. The diff shows what. ────────────────────────────────
# Size the message to the change:
#   mechanical edit ...... subject line alone
#   small single change .. a sentence or two
#   ordinary fix/feature . one or two short paragraphs
#   large refactor ....... two or three
#
# A message longer than the change warrants is evidence the commit should have
# been two. Reach for splitting before reaching for more prose.
#
# Durable reasoning belongs in a comment next to the code, where rebases cannot
# lose it. The body carries what a reverter needs.
#
# ── Before committing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   git diff --cached          # is this one reviewable decision?
#   git show --stat HEAD       # afterwards: did it contain what you meant?
#
# Trailers (optional):
#   Proportionality: <why this message needs unusual length>
#   Co-Authored-By: Name <email>
